      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can do this by dividing 91 by the smallest prime number, which is 2, and continuing with the next prime numbers until we can no longer divide evenly.\n\n91 ÷ 2 = 45.5 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 3 = 30.33 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 5 = 18.2 (not divisible)\n91 ÷ 7 = 13 (divisible)\n\nSince 91 can be divided by 7, we have found a prime factor. Now we can write the prime factorization of 91 as 7 × 13.\n\nNext, we use the formula for finding the sum of all divisors of a number based on its prime factorization. If a number n has the prime factorization n = p₁^a₁ × p₂^a₂ × ... × pₙ^aₙ, then the sum of all divisors of n can be found using the formula:\n\nSum of divisors = (1 + p₁ + p₁² + ... + p₁^a₁)(1 + p₂ + p₂² + ... + p₂^a₂)...(1 + pₙ + pₙ² + ... + pₙ^aₙ)\n\nFor our number 91, the prime factorization is 7 × 13, so we plug this into the formula:\n\nSum of divisors = (1 + 7)(1 + 13)\nSum of divisors = (8)(14)\n\nNow we multiply the two numbers together to find the final sum:\n\nSum of divisors = 8 × 14 = 112\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 112.",
