      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. We can see that 91 is divisible by 7, so we can write:\n\n91 = 7 × 13\n\nNow, we can use the formula for finding the sum of divisors of a number. If a number has prime factorization p1^e1 × p2^e2 × ... × pn^en, then the sum of its divisors is given by:\n\n(Sum of divisors) = (1 + p1 + p1^2 + ... + p1^(e1-1)) × (1 + p2 + p2^2 + ... + p2^(e2-1)) × ... × (1 + pn + pn^2 + ... + pn^(en-1))\n\nUsing this formula, we can find the sum of divisors of 91:\n\n(Sum of divisors) = (1 + 7 + 7^2) × (1 + 13 + 13^2)\n(Sum of divisors) = (1 + 7 + 49) × (1 + 13 + 169)\n(Sum of divisors) = 57 × 183\n(Sum of divisors) = 10311\n\nTherefore, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 10311.",
